WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:02.940
SPEAKER 1: Let's see how
to deploy an ASP.NET app

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:07.430
on Google Compute Engine using
Cloud Tools for Visual Studio.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:10.400
First, go to Tools, and
Extensions and Updates

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.760
and install Google Cloud
Tools for Visual Studio.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:18.190
Once installed, go to Google
Cloud Tools and Manage Accounts

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:20.930
and add your Google
Cloud account.

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:26.920
Now go to Google Cloud Explorer
and select your project.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.430
And then create a
new ASP.NET instance.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.220
This opens Cloud Launcher, where
you can deploy a Compute Engine

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:36.570
instance with Windows
Server, IaaS, SQL Server,

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:39.580
and ASP.NET framework installed.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:41.890
Once Compute Engine
instance is ready,

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:44.440
create a new Windows user.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.900
Finally, right-click
on your ASP.NET app

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.750
and select Publish
to Google Cloud.

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:53.680
Select Compute Engine, choose
the VM instance and the Windows

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.260
account that you want
to use to publish.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:00.270
In a few seconds, your app will
be deployed to Compute Engine.

